{
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Why is Ankuram considered the best CBSE tuition centre in Hyderabad?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Parents rank us highly because we cap batches at 3–5 students, start every enrolment with a diagnostic test, and teach NCERT-first before moving to board-format mixed practice. With 496+ Google reviews at 4.8 stars, the results speak for themselves — but the real difference is that I know each student by name and track their error patterns week to week."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What classes do you offer CBSE tuition for?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We cover CBSE Class 6 through Class 12. Maths is available for all grades. Science (Physics, Chemistry, Biology combined) up to Class 10. Physics separately for Classes 11 and 12. Many of my students come from Bharatiya Vidya Bhavan, JHPS, DPS, Obul Reddy, and Meridian."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How many students are in each batch?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Never more than 5. Most batches run at 3–4 students. When a child needs serious foundation repair — say, Class 8 algebra gaps showing up in Class 10 — I sometimes run a batch of 2. Large coaching centres cannot do this; I deliberately keep my batch count low so every student gets corrected in class, not just in homework."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the diagnostic test and why is it required?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It is a 60-minute assessment costing ₹750, covering Maths and Science topics from the student's current grade and two grades below. I use it to find exactly where gaps started — not where the school syllabus currently is. Without this, tuition becomes generic repetition. The diagnostic tells me whether your child needs concept repair, speed work, or exam-writing discipline."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you offer online CBSE tuition?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. We run a hybrid model: online classes on weekdays and offline sessions at our Jubilee Hills centre on weekends. During online classes, students photograph their written work and share it on WhatsApp for real-time correction. CBSE rewards method marks, so passive watching does not work — active solving with immediate feedback does."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What are the fees for CBSE tuition?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Fees depend on grade, subject combination, and session frequency. I quote after the diagnostic because a Class 8 student needing algebra repair has a different plan than a Class 12 student preparing for board exams. The diagnostic costs ₹750 regardless. There are no hidden charges — you know the plan and the fee before you commit."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Where is Ankuram Tuition Centre located?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
