        {"@type":"Question","name":"Does ISC Maths have project work?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The ISC Maths syllabus specifies Paper I (Theory) and Paper II (Project Work) with 80 + 20 marks."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"What is the biggest unit in ISC Class 12 Maths?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Calculus carries the largest unit weightage in Class XII (35 marks out of 80 in theory)."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"How is ISC Physics assessed besides theory?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The syllabus includes theory (70) plus practical (15), project work (10), and practical file (5)."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"Are numericals really required across the ISC Physics syllabus?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — ISC Physics notes that numerical problems are included from all topics except where excluded or qualitative-only."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"My child is strong in Maths but weak in Physics numericals — what usually causes that?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often it is not 'bad at physics.' It is missing a consistent diagram-to-equation workflow and weak unit/dimension discipline, which ISC theory expects."}},
        {"@type":"Question","name":"Can an ISC student do CBSE/JEE-style practice alongside boards?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, but only after the board foundations are stable. ISC has its own distribution and project/practical commitments, so we schedule extra problem sets only when weekly consistency is in place."}}
      ]
    }

